{"uid":"36433cf914ceec89","name":"test_step_replans_own_check_exhausts_max_approaches_to_failed","fullName":"tests.test_deadline#test_step_replans_own_check_exhausts_max_approaches_to_failed","historyId":"70dc85cd03d3967549a069b4e790106b","time":{"start":1791880964109,"stop":1791880964114,"duration":5},"description":"`_step_replan`'s OWN read of the live budget (docstring site 1).\n\n    Reachable at this state only because the run already arrived at\n    `replan` from an edge that checked the SAME live field at an earlier\n    moment (`_step_review`'s/`_step_verdict_gate`'s own approach-left\n    edges both check `approach < self.cfg.max_approaches` before ever\n    transitioning to `replan`; the worker stagnation guard's uncured\n    `stagnation_exhausted` edge, `loop.py:9584`, transitions to `replan`\n    with no approach check of its own at all, relying on `_step_replan`\n    to be the one that actually decides) -- a live `PATCH /config/budget`\n    lowering `maxApproaches` between that earlier decision and this\n    dispatch is exactly why two separate reads of one live field exist.\n    Seeded directly at `approach == max_approaches` (the post-PATCH\n    shape), `_step_replan()` must read the CURRENT value, not one carried\n    from whichever edge put the run in `replan`, and take `budget_or_\n    approach_exhausted` straight to the ordinary `failed` tail through\n    `_finish_tail_unverified()` -- never `_finish_timed_out()`, which is\n    what task 011's `_budget_exhausted_tail` flag would route it through\n    if this edge ever started setting it.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>_step_replan</code>'s OWN read of the live budget (docstring site 1).</p>\n<pre><code>Reachable at this state only because the run already arrived at\n`replan` from an edge that checked the SAME live field at an earlier\nmoment (`_step_review`'s/`_step_verdict_gate`'s own approach-left\nedges both check `approach &lt; self.cfg.max_approaches` before ever\ntransitioning to `replan`; the worker stagnation guard's uncured\n`stagnation_exhausted` edge, `loop.py:9584`, transitions to `replan`\nwith no approach check of its own at all, relying on `_step_replan`\nto be the one that actually decides) -- a live `PATCH /config/budget`\nlowering `maxApproaches` between that earlier decision and this\ndispatch is exactly why two separate reads of one live field exist.\nSeeded directly at `approach == max_approaches` (the post-PATCH\nshape), `_step_replan()` must read the CURRENT value, not one carried\nfrom whichever edge put the run in `replan`, and take `budget_or_\napproach_exhausted` straight to the ordinary `failed` tail through\n`_finish_tail_unverified()` -- never `_finish_timed_out()`, which is\nwhat task 011's `_budget_exhausted_tail` flag would route it through\nif this edge ever started setting it.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795037,"stop":1791880795037,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795038,"stop":1791880795038,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791880964092,"stop":1791880964097,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791880964092,"stop":1791880964092,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmen